WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.090
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.360 --> 01:34.920
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.200 --> 01:37.759
[Episode 49]

4
01:38.430 --> 01:40.070
Today, I want to announce a

5
01:40.560 --> 01:42.430
decision made by the

6
01:42.890 --> 01:44.289
Central Military Commission.

7
01:44.680 --> 01:48.509
The Generalissimo's headquarters will be relocated from Wuchang to Chongqing,

8
01:49.070 --> 01:51.430
and a group of military and political officials will be dispatched

9
01:51.870 --> 01:54.120
to help reorganize the Sichuan Army,

10
01:54.590 --> 01:56.280
in order to effectively and comprehensively

11
01:56.590 --> 01:58.560
improve their combat capabilities.

12
01:59.560 --> 02:02.010
Gentlemen, we are here today

13
02:02.070 --> 02:03.920
to commemorate the late Premier...

14
02:03.940 --> 02:04.780
Fucheng (Liu Xiang),

15
02:05.280 --> 02:09.470
Chiang is getting more and more greedy.

16
02:09.910 --> 02:11.590
If he puts down roots here,

17
02:12.360 --> 02:14.030
he will soon blossom and bear fruit.

18
02:15.000 --> 02:16.320
Can you really tolerate this?

19
02:17.560 --> 02:18.630
Uncle,

20
02:19.400 --> 02:21.430
if you were sitting in my position,

21
02:21.579 --> 02:22.780
could you tolerate it?

22
02:22.860 --> 02:25.350
[Liu Wenhui, Commander-in-Chief of the KMT Sichuan-Xikang Border Defense Army, Commander of the 24th Army]

23
02:23.430 --> 02:25.000
Right now, the greatest enemy is the Communist Army.

24
02:25.390 --> 02:28.210
[Liu Xiang, Commander-in-Chief of the Kuomintang Sichuan "Communist Suppression" Forces and Chairman of the Sichuan Provincial Government]

25
02:25.590 --> 02:27.000
Once the Communist Army marches south

26
02:27.280 --> 02:29.030
and captures our Western Sichuan Plain,

27
02:29.120 --> 02:30.680
they will be raiding our home base.

28
02:31.100 --> 02:32.420
Only by destroying the Communist Army

29
02:33.079 --> 02:35.280
can we have the capital to maneuver.

30
02:36.120 --> 02:37.710
With Sichuan stabilized,

31
02:38.190 --> 02:40.030
the country will be free of worries.

32
02:44.030 --> 02:44.870
It's over.

33
02:57.630 --> 02:59.110
The Communist Army marching south

34
02:59.840 --> 03:01.360
won't accomplish much.

35
03:01.790 --> 03:03.400
As for the Communist Army in northern Shaanxi,

36
03:04.630 --> 03:06.110
I actually want to let

37
03:06.750 --> 03:08.590
the Northeast Army clash with them

38
03:09.520 --> 03:10.750
to see the outcome.

39
03:12.000 --> 03:13.510
However, as for He Long's troops,

40
03:14.560 --> 03:16.070
it is time to finish them off.

41
03:16.930 --> 03:18.079
This is the purpose of making you

42
03:18.100 --> 03:20.100
the Chief of Staff of the Yichang Headquarters,

43
03:20.680 --> 03:21.960
which you should be aware of.

44
03:22.070 --> 03:23.070
I am aware.

45
03:23.710 --> 03:24.680
I have already drafted

46
03:24.710 --> 03:26.000
a new plan for a massive encirclement and suppression campaign.

47
03:26.120 --> 03:27.590
We plan to use 130 regiments,

48
03:27.610 --> 03:28.360
with about 200,000 troops,

49
03:28.560 --> 03:29.960
to gradually compress He Long's forces into

50
03:30.090 --> 03:33.730
[Chen Cheng, Chief of Staff and Acting Director of the Yichang Headquarters]

51
03:30.190 --> 03:31.190
the narrow areas of Longshan, Yongshun,

52
03:31.310 --> 03:32.590
and Sangzhi,

53
03:32.610 --> 03:33.850
in an attempt to wipe them out in one fell swoop.

54
03:34.430 --> 03:35.590
Good.

55
03:37.190 --> 03:40.240
Now that the majority of the Communist Army has gone north,

56
03:40.470 --> 03:42.030
the center of the Communist suppression campaign

57
03:42.410 --> 03:43.520
has also shifted north accordingly.

58
03:43.870 --> 03:44.870
On the southern bank of the Yangtze River,

59
03:44.920 --> 03:46.600
only this main force remains.

60
03:47.190 --> 03:49.150
He Long is a cunning commander,

61
03:49.710 --> 03:51.910
and Sangzhi is his old lair.

62
03:52.470 --> 03:53.910
Therefore, we cannot let him be

63
03:54.400 --> 03:55.840
and allow him to run increasingly rampant.

64
03:55.890 --> 03:57.260
The suppression operation

65
03:57.329 --> 03:58.400
should be carried out sooner rather than later.

66
03:58.940 --> 03:59.760
Yes, sir.

67
04:02.600 --> 04:06.340
[Dushuiping, Shimen County, Hunan]

68
04:04.170 --> 04:05.050
Currently,

69
04:05.750 --> 04:06.990
the Hunan and Hubei armies

70
04:07.240 --> 04:09.630
have already constructed blockhouses to our south, west,

71
04:09.320 --> 04:11.350
[He Long, Commander of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

72
04:09.910 --> 04:11.590
and north.

73
04:12.150 --> 04:13.800
Sun Lianzhong's column of the Central Army

74
04:14.190 --> 04:15.750
and Fan Songfu's column

75
04:15.960 --> 04:17.430
are serving as the main attacking forces.

76
04:17.470 --> 04:20.209
[Ren Bishi, Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee, Political Commissar of the 2nd Red Army Corps]

77
04:17.800 --> 04:21.070
From Jinshi, Lizhou, and the areas to the north,

78
04:21.510 --> 04:22.680
they are advancing towards us section by section

79
04:22.950 --> 04:24.630
using the tactic of blockhouses.

80
04:25.120 --> 04:26.160
I see that Chiang

81
04:26.430 --> 04:27.390
is trying to build a dam

82
04:27.630 --> 04:28.830
and drive the pigs into the pen.

83
04:29.130 --> 04:30.960
He's really out of his mind.

84
04:32.830 --> 04:33.720
Previously, we

85
04:33.870 --> 04:34.830
suggested to the Central Committee

86
04:35.020 --> 04:36.580
that we should move our main forces

87
04:36.720 --> 04:38.010
to the areas of Shiqian, Huangping, and Zhenyuan

88
04:38.130 --> 04:40.520
in eastern Guizhou,

89
04:40.840 --> 04:43.120
and strive to establish a revolutionary base there.

90
04:43.370 --> 04:46.270
[Xiao Ke, Commander of the 6th Red Army Corps]

91
04:43.750 --> 04:45.630
However, the Central Committee's response

92
04:45.950 --> 04:47.000
was somewhat ambiguous.

93
04:47.310 --> 04:48.120
Yes,

94
04:48.870 --> 04:49.720
on one hand,

95
04:49.740 --> 04:51.260
they disagreed with us fighting on the exterior lines.

96
04:51.800 --> 04:52.750
On the other hand, they said

97
04:53.040 --> 04:54.390
that everything should be based on the actual situation

98
04:54.570 --> 04:56.330
and decided by us.

99
04:57.870 --> 04:59.140
So how should we decide?

100
04:58.810 --> 05:00.680
[Wang Zhen, Political Commissar of 6th Red Army Corps]

101
04:59.800 --> 05:01.020
Since there is that last sentence,

102
05:01.390 --> 05:02.950
then we'll act according

103
05:03.270 --> 05:04.310
to the actual situation.

104
05:04.720 --> 05:06.560
After the Zunyi Conference, the Central Committee's directive stated

105
05:06.810 --> 05:08.930
that the overall policy is decisive defense,

106
05:09.090 --> 05:10.450
not simple defense.

107
05:11.120 --> 05:12.560
It's mobile warfare, not positional warfare.

108
05:12.950 --> 05:14.870
Now the enemy has made it clear

109
05:14.870 --> 05:16.310
that they want to fight a fortress and positional war with us.

110
05:16.630 --> 05:17.830
We can't just wait around

111
05:17.930 --> 05:19.170
for the enemy to trap us and attack.

112
05:19.450 --> 05:21.450
Comrade Bishi said it perfectly.

113
05:22.310 --> 05:23.040
We

114
05:23.060 --> 05:24.580
absolutely cannot meet the enemy head-on.

115
05:25.190 --> 05:26.160
I have an idea.

116
05:26.630 --> 05:27.750
Let's move our main forces

117
05:28.070 --> 05:30.000
back to the Sangzhi central area.

118
05:30.290 --> 05:32.050
We'll deploy our next moves

119
05:32.070 --> 05:33.590
based on changes in the enemy's situation.

120
05:33.920 --> 05:34.830
Comrades,

121
05:35.080 --> 05:36.720
we can't force ourselves

122
05:37.159 --> 05:39.240
into those rigid rules.

123
05:39.560 --> 05:41.760
Only flexibility provides a way out,

124
05:42.159 --> 05:43.040
doesn't it?

125
05:47.340 --> 05:49.460
After repeated discussions,

126
05:49.950 --> 05:51.270
the Military Commission Branch of the 2nd and 6th Red Army Corps

127
05:51.560 --> 05:52.920
ultimately decided not to follow

128
05:52.940 --> 05:54.530
Zhang Guotao's "Central" directives

129
05:54.890 --> 05:56.610
to stay in the Shimen area

130
05:56.710 --> 05:59.270
and fight positional or attrition warfare with the enemy.

131
06:00.080 --> 06:02.870
Instead, they concentrated their forces to return to the Sangzhi area,

132
06:03.440 --> 06:05.530
preparing for the next step of breaking out towards Guizhou

133
06:05.800 --> 06:06.720
and starting the Long March,

134
06:06.960 --> 06:08.870
thus laying a solid military foundation.

135
06:09.950 --> 06:12.040
On October 14, 1935,

136
06:12.360 --> 06:13.920
the northbound Shaanxi and Gansu Detachment

137
06:14.040 --> 06:15.980
marched to the Helianwan area,

138
06:16.050 --> 06:18.690
about to cross the watershed on the Shaanxi-Gansu border

139
06:19.070 --> 06:20.800
and enter Shaanxi province.

140
06:24.390 --> 06:26.240
Keep pushing, comrades!

141
06:26.910 --> 06:28.710
We've reached the top of the mountain!

142
06:29.490 --> 06:30.730
The main force has reached the summit!

143
06:31.240 --> 06:32.560
Keep pushing, comrades!

144
06:32.860 --> 06:35.190
As the vanguard of the whole army,

145
06:35.430 --> 06:36.870
we can't let others catch up with us,

146
06:37.070 --> 06:37.680
okay?

147
06:37.830 --> 06:38.630
Okay!

148
06:38.630 --> 06:39.360
Let's go!

149
06:39.510 --> 06:40.220
Hurry!

150
06:40.340 --> 06:41.640
Keep pushing. Keep pushing!

151
06:45.080 --> 06:46.080
Comrades,

152
06:47.000 --> 06:48.630
today is October 14.

153
06:49.390 --> 06:50.950
Last year on October 16,

154
06:51.700 --> 06:53.110
our 4th Red Regiment

155
06:53.170 --> 06:54.530
just crossed the Yudu River,

156
06:54.970 --> 06:57.000
starting our first day of the Long March.

157
06:57.130 --> 06:59.490
It's almost exactly one year. It really hasn't been easy!

158
06:59.560 --> 07:02.040
We've traveled across more than half of China on this journey, right?

159
07:02.210 --> 07:04.260
Someone calculated it; it's over 20,000 li!

160
07:04.440 --> 07:05.430
Is it really that far?

161
07:05.460 --> 07:06.280
Yes, it is.

162
07:07.220 --> 07:08.390
Then who remembers

163
07:08.410 --> 07:10.880
how many rivers we've crossed and mountains we've climbed?

164
07:11.080 --> 07:14.110
I remember, there's the Yudu River, Xiang River,

165
07:14.180 --> 07:17.510
Wujiang River, Chishui River, Jinsha River, and Dadu River!

166
07:17.530 --> 07:19.930
I heard if we keep heading north, we'll reach the Yellow River.

167
07:20.160 --> 07:22.310
There are even more mountains! Mount Laoshanjie

168
07:22.440 --> 07:24.790
was so steep that I had to climb on all fours.

169
07:24.810 --> 07:27.370
The big mountains in Guizhou are too many to count.

170
07:27.810 --> 07:29.250
I remember crossing Jiajin Mountain.

171
07:29.280 --> 07:30.350
When we went down the mountain,

172
07:30.370 --> 07:32.130
we slid down one after another.

173
07:32.890 --> 07:34.510
Many people plunged headfirst into the snowdrifts,

174
07:34.700 --> 07:36.290
leaving only their legs sticking out.

175
07:37.040 --> 07:37.870
I remember!

176
07:38.110 --> 07:39.470
Later, we pulled them out one by one,

177
07:39.500 --> 07:40.640
like pulling turnips!

178
07:44.050 --> 07:46.360
Lazikou counts as crossing a mountain too, right?

179
07:46.490 --> 07:48.720
It does. That area is called the Minshan Mountains.

180
07:49.370 --> 07:50.420
And there's Mount Liupan.

181
07:50.560 --> 07:53.390
After crossing Mount Liupan, it's all gullies and ridges.

182
07:54.220 --> 07:56.290
I wonder if Commander Geng's camera

183
07:56.520 --> 07:58.790
captured all these mountains and rivers.

184
07:58.900 --> 08:00.780
How could he have that many photographic plates?

185
08:00.900 --> 08:02.730
Even if he had them, he'd be reluctant to use them!

186
08:03.080 --> 08:04.110
Taking a picture

187
08:04.130 --> 08:05.480
is like cutting off a piece of his flesh!

188
08:05.720 --> 08:06.160
Right.

189
08:06.180 --> 08:07.310
He only took a group photo for us

190
08:07.330 --> 08:08.590
in Songkan.

191
08:09.420 --> 08:11.070
And that was taken by Commander Huang!

192
08:11.090 --> 08:13.050
At the time, everyone looked miserable.

193
08:13.140 --> 08:15.230
Commander Huang said one sentence and made us all laugh!

194
08:15.610 --> 08:17.850
You've walked so far. It's admirable.

195
08:17.970 --> 08:19.290
Kid, don't worry.

196
08:19.490 --> 08:21.690
You just joined the army; the road is still long.

197
08:21.950 --> 08:23.950
Commissar, once we reach Shaanxi and Gansu,

198
08:24.380 --> 08:25.770
does that mean we've finally won?

199
08:26.070 --> 08:27.680
It can only be considered a victory for this phase.

200
08:28.040 --> 08:29.870
We are still far from final victory!

201
08:30.800 --> 08:31.560
Comrades!

202
08:31.920 --> 08:32.870
When the revolution is victorious,

203
08:33.200 --> 08:34.440
what do you all want to do?

204
08:34.630 --> 08:35.789
I want to continue being a Red Army soldier.

205
08:36.360 --> 08:37.360
I want to be a Red Army soldier for the rest of my life,

206
08:37.789 --> 08:38.860
protecting the fruits of our victory.

207
08:38.890 --> 08:40.600
Good, good.

208
08:41.120 --> 08:42.820
Company Commander Wang, what do you want to do?

209
08:43.150 --> 08:44.960
I want to go abroad and have a look.

210
08:45.440 --> 08:46.320
Where?

211
08:46.600 --> 08:47.790
To the Soviet Union,

212
08:48.080 --> 08:48.910
to Moscow.

213
08:49.000 --> 08:50.900
Maybe I'll even get to see Comrade Stalin.

214
08:51.100 --> 08:52.100
Wang Youcai,

215
08:52.300 --> 08:53.230
will Comrade Stalin

216
08:53.250 --> 08:54.840
be able to understand your Cantonese accent?

217
08:55.670 --> 08:57.150
It doesn't matter if he understands or not;

218
08:57.150 --> 08:58.840
either way, I'm going to eat many loaves of dalieba.

219
08:59.050 --> 09:00.210
What's dalieba?

220
09:00.790 --> 09:02.200
It's that foreign bread.

221
09:03.070 --> 09:05.030
Yun Guichuan, what are your plans?

222
09:05.760 --> 09:07.160
First I'll go back to my hometown in Banqiao Town,

223
09:07.440 --> 09:08.480
then take my dad

224
09:08.790 --> 09:09.720
to Zunyi City

225
09:09.750 --> 09:10.720
and open an eatery.

226
09:11.240 --> 09:12.480
We'll sell mutton rice noodles.

227
09:13.120 --> 09:14.600
When the time comes, if our comrades go there to eat noodle soup,

228
09:14.790 --> 09:15.630
I won't charge you a dime.

229
09:16.230 --> 09:17.240
Great!

230
09:17.260 --> 09:17.910
I'll provide for you all!

231
09:17.930 --> 09:19.000
Great!

232
09:19.300 --> 09:20.210
Company Commander,

233
09:20.240 --> 09:21.920
what will you do when the revolution is victorious?

234
09:22.000 --> 09:22.720
Me?

235
09:22.840 --> 09:25.670
Right next to your mutton noodle shop,

236
09:26.140 --> 09:27.450
I'll open a Guokui shop,

237
09:27.480 --> 09:28.660
specializing in Guokui this big.

238
09:28.680 --> 09:30.360
-Big enough to stuff Yun to death! -Company Commander,

239
09:30.360 --> 09:32.110
that's old news. Why are you still bringing it up?

240
09:46.360 --> 09:47.120
What's going on?

241
09:47.270 --> 09:48.550
Reporting to the Regiment Commander and Commissar!

242
09:48.760 --> 09:49.480
In the village ahead,

243
09:49.480 --> 09:50.630
we spotted 7 or 8 armed landlords

244
09:50.880 --> 09:51.950
running into an earthen enclosure.

245
09:52.200 --> 09:53.010
Only 7 or 8?

246
09:53.050 --> 09:53.590
Yes.

247
09:57.910 --> 09:59.670
Regiment Commander, Commissar,

248
09:59.960 --> 10:01.080
we've been marching for days.

249
10:01.200 --> 10:03.080
Let me take the First Platoon to stretch our legs.

250
10:04.240 --> 10:04.920
Alright.

251
10:05.290 --> 10:06.640
Make it quick and stay safe.

252
10:07.240 --> 10:07.910
Yes, sir!

253
10:08.510 --> 10:09.600
First Platoon, follow me!

254
10:09.660 --> 10:10.290
Yes, sir!

255
10:32.280 --> 10:33.000
Company Commander,

256
10:33.130 --> 10:34.610
they're right inside that earthen enclosure.

257
10:46.130 --> 10:47.560
Listen up, people inside!

258
10:48.120 --> 10:49.670
We are the Workers' and Peasants' Red Army.

259
10:49.830 --> 10:51.560
Come out and surrender immediately!

260
10:51.790 --> 10:53.380
The Red Army treats prisoners well.

261
10:59.440 --> 11:00.560
I'll count to three.

262
11:00.700 --> 11:01.910
If you don't come out and surrender,

263
11:02.150 --> 11:03.390
I'll throw a grenade

264
11:03.520 --> 11:04.950
and blow you all to bits!

265
11:06.030 --> 11:07.240
One!

266
11:09.960 --> 11:11.080
Two!

267
11:13.370 --> 11:14.750
You won't shed a tear until you see the coffin!

268
11:15.090 --> 11:16.040
Open fire!

269
11:27.640 --> 11:28.430
Red Army!

270
11:28.460 --> 11:29.390
Comrades!

271
11:29.410 --> 11:30.580
We surrender!

272
11:31.800 --> 11:34.650
We surrender! We surrender!

273
11:35.510 --> 11:36.510
Throw down your guns!

274
11:37.110 --> 11:37.870
Hurry!

275
11:38.730 --> 11:41.400
Stop shooting. We surrender!

276
11:43.610 --> 11:45.800
Stop shooting! Stop shooting!

277
11:46.720 --> 11:48.120
Surrender! Surrender! Surrender!

278
11:48.240 --> 11:48.840
We surrender!

279
11:48.840 --> 11:50.150
Confiscate their weapons now!

280
11:50.740 --> 11:51.890
Don't shoot!

281
11:56.430 --> 11:58.120
Surrender! Surrender!

282
12:13.890 --> 12:14.860
Company Commander!

283
12:25.760 --> 12:26.520
Medic!

284
12:26.730 --> 12:28.010
Quick, go find the Medic!

285
12:42.590 --> 12:43.790
Company Commander, hold on!

286
12:43.940 --> 12:45.020
I'll take you to the Medic.

287
13:01.240 --> 13:02.530
Company Commander, hang in there!

288
13:05.920 --> 13:08.240
Medic!

289
13:13.510 --> 13:14.960
Medic!

290
13:20.330 --> 13:22.760
Medic!

291
13:24.790 --> 13:27.120
It hurts! It hurts!

292
13:34.240 --> 13:36.670
Medic!

293
13:44.130 --> 13:44.770
Company Commander!

294
13:45.490 --> 13:46.760
It's yours now!

295
13:48.730 --> 13:51.710
[Mao Zhenhua, Company Commander of the 1st Company, 4th Detachment, Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment]

296
13:49.270 --> 13:50.120
Hang in there!

297
13:50.390 --> 13:51.800
The Medic is coming right away.

298
13:52.190 --> 13:54.220
Company Commander, hold on a little longer!

299
13:54.990 --> 13:55.900
Company Commander!

300
13:56.960 --> 13:58.120
Company Commander!

301
13:59.300 --> 14:00.490
Company Commander!

302
14:02.510 --> 14:03.720
Company Commander!

303
14:04.380 --> 14:07.920
Company Commander!

304
14:14.420 --> 14:18.050
[Wuqi Town, Bao'an County, Shaanxi Province]

305
14:16.030 --> 14:17.770
Fellow villagers, is anyone home?

306
14:17.800 --> 14:18.720
Is anyone there?

307
14:19.630 --> 14:19.960
Fellow villagers!

308
14:19.960 --> 14:21.030
We are the Red Army.

309
14:21.360 --> 14:21.670
Is anyone there?

310
14:21.670 --> 14:22.480
We are the Red Army.

311
14:22.960 --> 14:23.790
Fellow villagers!

312
14:23.870 --> 14:25.030
Fellow villagers, we are the Red Army.

313
14:25.030 --> 14:26.350
Is anyone there? Is anyone there?

314
14:26.430 --> 14:27.350
Fellow villagers!

315
14:27.790 --> 14:28.720
Fellow villagers, is anyone there?

316
14:28.720 --> 14:29.600
Fellow villagers!

317
14:29.870 --> 14:30.750
Is anyone there?

318
14:30.870 --> 14:31.750
Is anyone there?

319
14:32.430 --> 14:33.840
Don't be afraid. We are the Red Army.

320
14:33.860 --> 14:35.100
Is anyone home?

321
14:35.230 --> 14:36.070
Fellow villagers!

322
14:36.440 --> 14:37.270
Is anyone there?

323
14:37.270 --> 14:38.670
Fellow villagers, are you home?

324
14:38.690 --> 14:39.810
We are the Red Army.

325
14:40.520 --> 14:41.440
We've been marching for so long.

326
14:41.790 --> 14:43.590
Comrade Zedong, look.

327
14:45.000 --> 14:46.150
Xi Zhongxun?

328
14:46.670 --> 14:48.510
Comrade Jia Tuofu has introduced this comrade before.

329
14:51.510 --> 14:53.240
Fellow villagers, is anyone there?

330
14:54.030 --> 14:54.880
Don't be afraid.

331
14:54.910 --> 14:57.270
It seems we have arrived.

332
14:57.680 --> 14:58.640
Report!

333
15:00.670 --> 15:01.960
Chairman Mao, Vice Chairman Zhou.

334
15:02.440 --> 15:03.870
We found people on the nearby mountains.

335
15:03.890 --> 15:05.200
They might be villagers from the nearby town.

336
15:05.600 --> 15:06.600
They ran away as soon as we got close.

337
15:07.960 --> 15:09.360
As long as it's Soviet territory,

338
15:09.920 --> 15:12.240
there is no reason to run away upon seeing the Red Army.

339
15:13.220 --> 15:14.370
It seems they have misunderstood.

340
15:14.400 --> 15:15.860
[Liang Xingchu, Commander of the directly affiliated reconnaissance company of the 1st Column of the Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment]

341
15:14.790 --> 15:15.510
Tell the comrades,

342
15:15.530 --> 15:16.200
without permission,

343
15:16.240 --> 15:17.920
no one is allowed to enter the villagers' courtyards.

344
15:18.360 --> 15:19.390
Shout to the mountains,

345
15:19.510 --> 15:21.360
and tell the villagers that we are the Red Army.

346
15:21.960 --> 15:22.650
Yes, sir!

347
15:25.870 --> 15:27.470
We are the Red Army!

348
15:32.070 --> 15:32.920
You guys,

349
15:33.270 --> 15:34.030
come with me.

350
15:34.050 --> 15:34.640
Yes, sir!

351
16:09.200 --> 16:10.200
Report!

352
16:12.150 --> 16:13.150
Report!

353
16:14.200 --> 16:15.550
Chairman Mao, Vice Chairman Zhou.

354
16:15.810 --> 16:17.290
We've found our local cadre comrade.

355
16:17.670 --> 16:18.430
Comrade Zhang Mingke,

356
16:18.670 --> 16:20.070
these two are our commanders.

357
16:19.850 --> 16:23.600
[Zhang Mingke, Captain of the Bao'an County Guerrilla Force]

358
16:20.670 --> 16:21.630
Greetings, Commanders!

359
16:22.110 --> 16:24.590
I am Zhang Mingke, Captain of the Bao'an County Guerrilla Force.

360
16:25.510 --> 16:27.030
Hello, Captain Zhang.

361
16:27.240 --> 16:28.240
Commanders!

362
16:29.030 --> 16:29.670
Commanders!

363
16:29.700 --> 16:30.460
Hello, Captain Zhang.

364
16:30.590 --> 16:32.070
We've been waiting so long for you!

365
16:33.320 --> 16:34.350
I just want to ask,

366
16:34.550 --> 16:38.150
which one of you is Chief Zhu Mao?

367
16:41.190 --> 16:42.440
We do have Zhu Mao,

368
16:42.840 --> 16:44.200
but Zhu and Mao are two people.

369
16:44.720 --> 16:45.870
I am one of them.

370
16:46.000 --> 16:46.710
I am Mao,

371
16:47.790 --> 16:48.790
and my name is Mao Zedong.

372
16:49.130 --> 16:49.920
This is our

373
16:49.960 --> 16:51.510
Chairman Mao of the Chinese Soviet Republic,

374
16:51.510 --> 16:53.360
and this is Vice Chairman Zhou of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

375
16:56.080 --> 16:57.200
Chairman Mao.

376
16:59.150 --> 17:00.630
Greetings, Chairman Mao!

377
17:00.750 --> 17:01.500
Glad to meet you, comrade.

378
17:03.150 --> 17:04.200
Greetings, Vice Chairman Zhou.

379
17:05.650 --> 17:06.650
Comrade Zhang Mingke,

380
17:06.829 --> 17:08.970
why is there no one in our town?

381
17:10.440 --> 17:11.640
Our scouts

382
17:11.790 --> 17:12.960
saw a troop coming,

383
17:13.510 --> 17:14.560
didn't clarify the situation,

384
17:14.589 --> 17:15.720
and thought it was the Northeast Army,

385
17:16.109 --> 17:17.200
so they evacuated the surrounding masses

386
17:17.349 --> 17:18.400
to the mountains.

387
17:18.680 --> 17:20.400
I have already sent people to call them back.

388
17:20.530 --> 17:21.480
It was a misunderstanding.

389
17:22.240 --> 17:24.960
Does everyone know the news about the Northern Shaanxi Red Army?

390
17:25.720 --> 17:26.440
Yes, yes.

391
17:26.790 --> 17:27.829
Just half a month ago,

392
17:28.349 --> 17:29.790
our Northern Shaanxi 15th Red Army Corps

393
17:30.240 --> 17:32.310
won a great victory in Laoshan.

394
17:32.510 --> 17:34.400
We wiped out a division of the Kuomintang's

395
17:34.430 --> 17:35.300
Northeast Army!

396
17:35.330 --> 17:36.370
The 15th Red Army Corps?

397
17:37.510 --> 17:38.960
Our Northern Shaanxi 15th Red Army Corps

398
17:39.240 --> 17:40.510
was formed after our Northern Shaanxi Red Army

399
17:40.790 --> 17:43.200
joined forces with the 25th Red Army.

400
17:43.490 --> 17:45.210
The Corps Commander is Xu Haidong,

401
17:45.240 --> 17:46.610
and the Political Commissar is Cheng Zihua.

402
17:47.070 --> 17:48.170
It seems the 25th Red Army

403
17:48.240 --> 17:49.740
arrived in northern Shaanxi before the Central Committee.

404
17:50.830 --> 17:51.700
Let me ask you,

405
17:52.270 --> 17:55.150
what position does Comrade Liu Zhidan hold

406
17:55.430 --> 17:56.800
in the 15th Red Army Corps?

407
18:07.400 --> 18:08.510
Do you happen to know

408
18:08.880 --> 18:10.930
where Comrade Liu Zhidan is right now?

409
18:15.510 --> 18:16.680
Comrade Zhang Mingke,

410
18:17.160 --> 18:18.510
is there any difficulty?

411
18:19.110 --> 18:20.590
It's okay. Don't be afraid.

412
18:24.550 --> 18:25.550
Reporting to Chairman Mao,

413
18:26.070 --> 18:28.400
the base area is carrying out a purge of counter-revolutionaries,

414
18:28.830 --> 18:30.070
and Comrade Liu Zhidan

415
18:30.720 --> 18:31.590
has been arrested.

416
18:31.830 --> 18:32.620
Arrested?

417
18:33.900 --> 18:34.900
When did this happen?

418
18:35.110 --> 18:36.070
It's been a few days.

419
18:36.270 --> 18:37.200
Where is he being held?

420
18:37.790 --> 18:38.750
In Wayaobu.

421
18:38.880 --> 18:40.620
Many others are locked up with him.

422
18:40.790 --> 18:42.080
The Chairman of our Soviet,

423
18:42.110 --> 18:43.070
Comrade Zhongxun,

424
18:43.310 --> 18:44.750
is also locked up with them.

425
18:45.030 --> 18:46.480
Xi Zhongxun who wrote the public notice?

426
18:49.680 --> 18:51.240
Do you know the specific situation right now?

427
18:51.480 --> 18:53.350
I'm not too clear about the situation,

428
18:53.590 --> 18:55.060
but I simply cannot believe

429
18:55.590 --> 18:56.550
that Comrade Liu Zhidan

430
18:56.750 --> 18:58.400
and Comrade Xi Zhongxun are counter-revolutionaries.

431
18:58.830 --> 19:00.700
They are the leaders

432
19:00.720 --> 19:01.680
of our revolution in northern Shaanxi.

433
19:02.880 --> 19:05.270
This matter must be investigated as soon as possible.

434
19:05.830 --> 19:07.310
Killing people is not like cutting chives.

435
19:07.510 --> 19:09.030
Chives can grow back after being cut,

436
19:09.310 --> 19:11.470
but a fallen head cannot.

437
19:12.640 --> 19:13.920
Execution must be halted first.

438
19:14.250 --> 19:14.920
Yes.

439
19:17.400 --> 19:18.350
Chairman Mao!

440
19:21.000 --> 19:22.000
Chairman Mao, Vice Chairman Zhou!

441
19:22.360 --> 19:23.360
Urgent enemy intelligence!

442
19:24.590 --> 19:25.310
Speak.

443
19:25.450 --> 19:27.080
The Kuomintang's 6th Division under Bai Fengxiang

444
19:27.200 --> 19:29.070
and the cavalry of the two Mas from Ningxia have caught up.

445
19:28.250 --> 19:32.210
[Ye Jianying, Chief of Staff of the Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment and Commander of the 3rd Column]

446
19:29.350 --> 19:30.270
They are attempting to annihilate us,

447
19:30.520 --> 19:32.280
and have now massed around Helianwan.

448
19:32.680 --> 19:33.590
Helianwan?

449
19:34.110 --> 19:35.270
That's not far from here.

450
19:36.750 --> 19:37.790
We cannot bring this tail

451
19:38.240 --> 19:39.510
into the northern Shaanxi base area.

452
19:39.920 --> 19:40.750
Comrade Jianying,

453
19:41.160 --> 19:42.960
send a telegram to Peng Dehuai immediately

454
19:43.310 --> 19:44.310
and tell him to rush over as soon as possible.

455
19:44.750 --> 19:45.880
We need to discuss the battle plan.

456
19:46.240 --> 19:46.860
Yes.

457
19:47.880 --> 19:48.720
Comrade Zhang Mingke,

458
19:48.980 --> 19:50.720
could you explain to us

459
19:50.750 --> 19:51.480
in as much detail as possible

460
19:51.480 --> 19:53.400
the situation of Comrades Liu Zhidan and Xi Zhongxun?

461
19:53.520 --> 19:54.090
Sure.

462
19:54.470 --> 19:55.960
Come on.

463
20:02.100 --> 20:03.140
Everyone knows

464
20:03.790 --> 20:05.110
that in plain areas,

465
20:05.680 --> 20:07.310
infantry indeed has a hard time fighting cavalry.

466
20:07.920 --> 20:09.030
However, on our way here,

467
20:09.270 --> 20:10.320
I observed

468
20:10.480 --> 20:11.880
the terrain around Wuqi Town.

469
20:12.200 --> 20:13.160
Fighting cavalry here

470
20:13.350 --> 20:14.640
might not be impossible.

471
20:14.690 --> 20:15.420
Look,

472
20:15.620 --> 20:17.180
to enter Wuqi Town from the outside,

473
20:17.550 --> 20:18.790
one must pass through these 3 river valleys.

474
20:18.960 --> 20:20.720
Between the first and second valleys

475
20:20.880 --> 20:23.310
lies a large ridge with deep ravines and narrow roads.

476
20:24.310 --> 20:25.350
Cavalry moves fast

477
20:25.550 --> 20:26.640
and has a strong impact,

478
20:26.990 --> 20:28.710
but they are also larger targets

479
20:29.240 --> 20:30.350
and require open terrain.

480
20:30.680 --> 20:32.070
Between these two valleys,

481
20:32.270 --> 20:33.640
they simply cannot deploy their formation.

482
20:33.790 --> 20:34.750
Such terrain, however,

483
20:35.310 --> 20:36.240
is exceptionally advantageous

484
20:36.590 --> 20:38.240
for us.

485
20:39.240 --> 20:39.920
Here,

486
20:40.270 --> 20:41.310
here,

487
20:41.790 --> 20:42.640
and here

488
20:43.270 --> 20:44.640
are all suitable for us to lay ambushes.

489
20:44.660 --> 20:46.420
Strike the enemy from a commanding height

490
20:48.880 --> 20:50.640
and lure them deep into a pocket ambush.

491
20:51.720 --> 20:52.510
Good.

492
20:52.620 --> 20:53.380
Peng,

493
20:53.830 --> 20:55.590
explain the combat deployment in more detail.

494
20:56.160 --> 20:58.240
First, the Cadre Regiment of the 3rd Column

495
20:59.000 --> 20:59.920
will lure the enemy in deep.

496
21:00.240 --> 21:02.880
The 1st Column will set an ambush at the front of the 3rd valley.

497
21:03.270 --> 21:06.160
The 2nd Column will ambush on the left flank of the 1st valley.

498
21:06.630 --> 21:08.910
The rest of the 3rd Column in the 3rd valley

499
21:09.110 --> 21:11.070
will monitor the enemies from the southwest

500
21:11.440 --> 21:13.000
and cover the 2nd Column's operations.

501
21:13.980 --> 21:14.980
Do you all agree?

502
21:15.640 --> 21:16.510
I have no objections.

503
21:16.830 --> 21:17.510
Peng,

504
21:17.790 --> 21:20.350
tomorrow I'll be on Platform Mountain,

505
21:20.920 --> 21:22.240
waiting for news of your victory.

506
21:22.880 --> 21:23.490
Good.

507
21:25.830 --> 21:30.090
[Platform Mountain, Wuqi Town, Shaanxi]

508
21:43.620 --> 21:48.260
[Wuligou Battlefield, outskirts of Wuqi Town, Shaanxi]

509
22:12.400 --> 22:13.680
I stayed up all night yesterday,

510
22:14.350 --> 22:15.110
so I'll sleep for a while.

511
22:15.440 --> 22:16.200
Yes.

512
22:26.790 --> 22:28.350
When the gunfire is heavy,

513
22:29.400 --> 22:30.450
do not wake me up.

514
22:31.640 --> 22:33.030
When the gunfire becomes sparse,

515
22:33.550 --> 22:34.590
you may wake me.

516
22:36.950 --> 22:37.600
Yes, sir.

517
24:20.480 --> 24:21.260
It stopped.

518
24:35.230 --> 24:36.270
Chairman Mao.

519
24:42.480 --> 24:43.310
Reporting to the Chairman.

520
24:43.440 --> 24:44.390
Commander Peng ordered me

521
24:44.510 --> 24:45.930
to report the frontline results to you.

522
24:45.960 --> 24:46.680
Speak.

523
24:46.830 --> 24:48.200
After a fierce battle, our army

524
24:48.480 --> 24:51.090
completely routed 3 regiments of the Kuomintang army

525
24:51.110 --> 24:52.920
and a cavalry regiment of Ma Hongbin.

526
24:52.950 --> 24:55.060
The remnants of the enemy retreated across the entire line.

527
24:55.380 --> 24:56.250
Preliminary statistics show

528
24:56.280 --> 24:57.810
that nearly a thousand enemy troops were killed, wounded, or captured.

529
24:57.940 --> 25:00.050
We also captured a large number of warhorses,

530
25:00.470 --> 25:02.330
light and heavy machine guns, and mortars.

531
25:02.640 --> 25:03.790
The exact numbers are being counted.

532
25:04.440 --> 25:05.920
Peng cut off this tail well;

533
25:07.230 --> 25:09.680
it can be considered a gift from us

534
25:10.000 --> 25:10.960
to the people of northern Shaanxi upon our arrival.

535
25:10.980 --> 25:11.650
Yes.

536
25:12.790 --> 25:13.440
Wu!

537
25:13.680 --> 25:14.090
Here.

538
25:14.120 --> 25:15.120
Bring the Four Treasures of the Study.

539
25:19.530 --> 25:20.280
Chairman.

540
26:06.760 --> 26:07.950
Commander Peng.

541
26:13.240 --> 26:14.000
Reporting to the Commander.

542
26:14.200 --> 26:16.010
I have reported the battle results to Chairman Mao.

543
26:17.790 --> 26:19.590
Chairman asked me to give it to you.

544
26:25.110 --> 26:26.880
Mountains are high, roads are long, and ravines are deep;

545
26:26.900 --> 26:28.170
a great army gallops far and wide.

546
26:28.750 --> 26:30.100
Who dares to draw their sword and mount their horse?

547
26:30.400 --> 26:32.030
None but my Great General Peng!

548
26:34.150 --> 26:34.940
Peng,

549
26:35.340 --> 26:37.380
this poem truly lives up to your name.

550
26:37.790 --> 26:39.070
I think it should be announced to the entire army.

551
26:55.790 --> 26:58.200
[The Heroic Red Army]

552
27:03.270 --> 27:04.830
Who dares to draw their sword and mount their horse?

553
27:05.410 --> 27:07.370
None but our heroic Red Army!

554
27:08.620 --> 27:11.010
On October 22, 1935,

555
27:11.780 --> 27:13.270
the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee

556
27:13.290 --> 27:15.600
held an enlarged meeting in Wuqi Town,

557
27:16.230 --> 27:17.840
approving the decision made by the Standing Committee

558
27:17.860 --> 27:19.540
of the Politburo at the Bangluo Town meeting

559
27:19.680 --> 27:21.870
to settle the Red Army in northern Shaanxi.

560
27:22.880 --> 27:24.030
The meeting also decided

561
27:24.390 --> 27:27.580
to send Jia Tuofu and Li Weihan, Minister of Local Work,

562
27:27.630 --> 27:28.710
ahead

563
27:29.270 --> 27:30.950
to find the northern Shaanxi Red Army

564
27:30.970 --> 27:33.210
and arrange the meeting of the two armies.

565
27:35.070 --> 27:39.190
[Red Army Hospital, Luo River, Shaanxi]

566
27:35.690 --> 27:36.860
Has he been running a fever the whole time?

567
27:38.280 --> 27:39.520
We've tried everything,

568
27:40.090 --> 27:41.160
but it just won't go down.

569
27:41.850 --> 27:42.850
He won't let anyone

570
27:43.080 --> 27:44.030
touch these three items of his.

571
27:44.440 --> 27:45.770
He gets anxious if anyone tries.

572
27:47.160 --> 27:48.710
These three are his treasures.

573
27:48.950 --> 27:49.880
This pocket watch

574
27:50.070 --> 27:51.110
was given by Vice Chairman Zhou.

575
27:51.550 --> 27:52.790
The gun was given by the Commander-in-Chief.

576
27:53.440 --> 27:54.440
And this axe

577
27:54.550 --> 27:55.480
has seen Chairman Mao.

578
27:55.540 --> 27:57.060
Everyone says your 4th Red Corps has it tough;

579
27:57.980 --> 27:59.180
seeing Commander Huang,

580
27:59.360 --> 28:00.560
I feel it even more deeply.

581
28:01.110 --> 28:02.160
When he first arrived,

582
28:02.280 --> 28:03.480
we washed his body for him,

583
28:03.960 --> 28:05.290
and both of his feet were covered in festering sores.

584
28:05.680 --> 28:06.920
From the sole of his left foot,

585
28:07.030 --> 28:10.590
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Red Regiment]

586
28:07.310 --> 28:08.640
we gouged out a small stone.

587
28:08.920 --> 28:10.510
We then found another one,

588
28:10.880 --> 28:12.200
which had grown into the flesh

589
28:13.200 --> 28:14.070
and couldn't be taken out.

590
28:16.750 --> 28:18.200
Our regiment walks a lot

591
28:18.640 --> 28:19.960
and it's always forced marches.

592
28:21.070 --> 28:22.240
The most extreme time,

593
28:22.640 --> 28:24.880
we covered 240 li in a single day and night.

594
28:30.450 --> 28:31.380
There is one more thing.

595
28:31.640 --> 28:32.390
What is it?

596
28:32.750 --> 28:33.680
The night before last,

597
28:33.880 --> 28:35.030
commander Huang was running a fever,

598
28:35.550 --> 28:36.480
and suddenly got up.

599
28:36.790 --> 28:37.930
He took his own quilt

600
28:37.950 --> 28:39.160
and covered a soldier with it.

601
28:39.510 --> 28:41.200
His two hands clenched tightly.

602
28:41.550 --> 28:42.790
We couldn't pull him away.

603
28:43.350 --> 28:44.480
He kept saying,

604
28:44.680 --> 28:45.400
"Cold.

605
28:46.200 --> 28:47.720
Rain can kill people."

606
28:48.110 --> 28:49.420
But when we asked him the next day,

607
28:49.810 --> 28:51.090
he couldn't remember anything at all.

608
28:53.640 --> 28:55.070
When our regiment crossed the grasslands,

609
28:55.880 --> 28:57.440
we lost over two hundred comrades.

610
29:22.780 --> 29:23.730
Yang.

611
29:24.190 --> 29:26.050
Huang, you're awake!

612
29:29.360 --> 29:31.590
I miss you so much.

613
29:33.620 --> 29:35.490
Has our regiment moved out?

614
29:35.920 --> 29:36.750
Soon.

615
29:37.070 --> 29:38.070
We'll arrive at Xiasiwan soon

616
29:38.090 --> 29:39.480
to join forces with the 15th Red Army Corps.

617
29:40.160 --> 29:41.400
That's great.

618
29:42.030 --> 29:43.200
After joining forces,

619
29:44.110 --> 29:46.110
our strength will grow.

620
29:47.310 --> 29:49.590
Didn't Chairman Mao say at the meeting

621
29:51.000 --> 29:52.850
that our current mission

622
29:53.590 --> 29:58.870
is to protect and expand the Northern Shaanxi Soviet Area?

623
30:00.040 --> 30:01.910
That's absolutely right.

624
30:02.990 --> 30:04.800
You still remember Chairman Mao's speech.

625
30:05.590 --> 30:07.640
Why wouldn't I remember?

626
30:08.570 --> 30:10.570
It was just a couple of days ago.

627
30:11.750 --> 30:13.160
And I also remember

628
30:13.510 --> 30:15.070
that after the assembly,

629
30:15.960 --> 30:18.030
Chairman Mao and Vice Chairman Zhou

630
30:18.510 --> 30:20.880
treated us to stewed mutton with radish.

631
30:21.670 --> 30:22.560
Oh boy,

632
30:23.070 --> 30:24.480
there were plenty of radishes

633
30:25.210 --> 30:26.450
but barely any mutton.

634
30:40.810 --> 30:41.640
Oh,

635
30:44.450 --> 30:46.620
look what I brought you!

636
30:48.660 --> 30:49.560
Apples!

637
30:52.380 --> 30:54.460
These are not easy to get.

638
30:55.980 --> 30:57.370
This big one is for you.

639
30:58.380 --> 30:59.680
They are all for you.

640
31:00.510 --> 31:04.010
[Huang Kaixiang, Commander of the 4th Red Regiment]

641
31:07.900 --> 31:09.660
How is it? Sweet?

642
31:33.260 --> 31:34.330
Still running a fever.

643
31:36.080 --> 31:38.600
Huang, when you recover and get discharged,

644
31:38.940 --> 31:39.690
I'll treat you

645
31:40.480 --> 31:42.590
to some real scalded-skin mutton.

646
32:10.450 --> 32:12.160
Huang, what are you doing?

647
32:14.220 --> 32:15.180
The chains are scalding.

648
32:15.810 --> 32:16.460
Fetch the door planks!

649
32:17.510 --> 32:18.510
What did you say?

650
32:19.680 --> 32:21.050
The chains are scalding.

651
32:21.590 --> 32:22.600
We need the door planks!

652
32:27.400 --> 32:29.350
In November 1935,

653
32:30.460 --> 32:33.070
Huang Kaixiang, suffering from severe typhoid,

654
32:33.090 --> 32:34.080
tragically passed away

655
32:34.850 --> 32:36.520
at the age of only 34.

656
32:38.070 --> 32:39.110
Huang Kaixiang

657
32:39.190 --> 32:41.800
was from Huangjia Village, Yiyang County, Jiangxi Province,

658
32:43.020 --> 32:44.970
joined the revolution in 1926,

659
32:45.660 --> 32:48.740
and served as Commander of the Northeastern Jiangxi Red Guard Regiment,

660
32:49.270 --> 32:52.160
Political Commissar of the 82nd Regiment of the 10th Red Army,

661
32:52.830 --> 32:55.380
Political Commissar of the 1st Division of the 1st Red Army Corps,

662
32:56.030 --> 32:58.110
and Commander of the 4th Red Regiment.

663
32:59.270 --> 33:00.960
His stories during the Long March

664
33:01.200 --> 33:03.720
were mostly recalled by General Yang Chengwu.

665
33:04.570 --> 33:06.170
In the Minxi dialect of Fujian,

666
33:06.210 --> 33:07.620
"Huang" and "Wang" are pronounced similarly.

667
33:07.980 --> 33:08.980
For a long time,

668
33:09.270 --> 33:11.560
military history recorded his name as Wang Kaixiang.

669
33:12.110 --> 33:14.640
It was not confirmed until the 1980s

670
33:14.810 --> 33:17.520
that the vanguard Regiment Commander during the Long March

671
33:17.730 --> 33:19.450
was named Huang Kaixiang.

672
33:21.770 --> 33:26.880
[Yulin Bridge]

673
33:22.310 --> 33:24.640
On October 25, 1935,

674
33:25.480 --> 33:26.720
to consolidate the Shaanxi-Gansu Revolutionary Base Area

675
33:26.750 --> 33:28.880
and welcome the arrival of the Central Red Army,

676
33:29.310 --> 33:31.200
the 15th Red Army Corps,

677
33:31.790 --> 33:34.070
launched an attack on the Northeast Army's

678
33:34.070 --> 33:36.960
619th Regiment, 107th Division stationed at Yulin Bridge.

679
33:37.480 --> 33:38.550
After fierce fighting,

680
33:38.790 --> 33:39.880
they annihilated the entire regiment

681
33:40.310 --> 33:42.760
and captured its commander, Gao Fuyuan.

682
33:41.960 --> 33:45.660
[Yulin Bridge, Shaanxi]

683
34:01.380 --> 34:02.590
Report your name and position.

684
34:05.830 --> 34:06.820
What's your name?

685
34:06.610 --> 34:08.510
[Gao Fuyuan, Commander of the 619th Regiment, 107th Division, 67th Corps of the Northeast Army]

686
34:07.670 --> 34:09.219
I am your ancestor.

687
34:09.940 --> 34:10.719
Han Xianchu.

688
34:13.510 --> 34:14.389
Ancestor?

689
34:14.989 --> 34:17.810
[Xu Haidong, Commander of the 15th Red Army Corps]

690
34:15.280 --> 34:16.710
That's quite a big name.

691
34:18.510 --> 34:20.030
My name isn't as big as yours.

692
34:21.030 --> 34:22.080
I am Xu Haidong.

693
34:24.400 --> 34:25.520
You are Xu Haidong?

694
34:25.550 --> 34:26.300
The one and only.

695
34:28.800 --> 34:29.760
Xu the Tiger.

696
34:29.920 --> 34:31.000
We are old acquaintances.

697
34:31.920 --> 34:34.800
I am Gao Fuyuan, Commander of the 619th Regiment.

698
34:36.400 --> 34:37.620
Quite a big shot indeed.

699
34:40.409 --> 34:41.920
Great ancestor.

700
34:47.110 --> 34:49.030
Commander Gao, you haven't eaten yet, have you?

701
34:49.440 --> 34:50.400
Sit down and eat with us.

702
35:14.820 --> 35:16.760
Drink some soup to warm yourself up.

703
35:19.760 --> 35:21.910
[Han Xianchu, Commander of the 1st Battalion, 225th Regiment, 15th Red Army Corps]

704
35:36.730 --> 35:38.210
Get him two more potatoes.

705
35:42.550 --> 35:44.150
A soldier can be killed, but not humiliated.

706
35:44.270 --> 35:45.170
Just shoot me.

707
35:45.900 --> 35:46.660
Right.

708
35:47.070 --> 35:48.830
You Red Army don't have many bullets,

709
35:49.880 --> 35:50.830
so beheading is fine too.

710
36:03.610 --> 36:05.290
So you're a "soldier", huh?

711
36:05.830 --> 36:07.060
Don't worry, Commander Gao.

712
36:07.530 --> 36:08.860
We won't humiliate you.

713
36:09.400 --> 36:11.400
You're injured, so we'll treat your wounds first.

714
36:11.760 --> 36:12.590
Han Xianchu!

715
36:12.970 --> 36:13.530
Here.

716
36:13.780 --> 36:14.610
Send someone to escort him away.

717
36:14.710 --> 36:15.220
Yes, sir.

718
36:19.730 --> 36:21.310
After you, great ancestor.

719
36:24.300 --> 36:25.140
Commander Gao,

720
36:26.450 --> 36:28.120
I've been fighting your Northeast Army

721
36:28.150 --> 36:29.070
for quite some years.

722
36:29.360 --> 36:30.710
Back in Hubei-Henan-Anhui,

723
36:30.900 --> 36:32.130
you never won once.

724
36:32.360 --> 36:34.020
Your 619th Regiment

725
36:34.250 --> 36:35.690
refuses to yield even after suffering heavily.

726
36:36.150 --> 36:37.800
Today you had such good fortifications,

727
36:37.820 --> 36:40.110
and your weapons and equipment are much better than before.

728
36:41.070 --> 36:42.150
You even had more bullets.

729
36:43.020 --> 36:44.500
But you still lost.

730
36:45.860 --> 36:46.930
Do you know why?

731
36:48.310 --> 36:49.980
Because the fighting spirit of your Northeast Army

732
36:50.000 --> 36:50.930
is getting worse and worse,

733
36:52.330 --> 36:53.440
as everyone

734
36:53.810 --> 36:55.570
no longer wants Chinese to fight against Chinese.

735
37:03.370 --> 37:04.340
Take him away.

736
37:04.490 --> 37:05.180
Let's go.

737
37:10.510 --> 37:11.820
What a waste of food.

738
37:14.640 --> 37:15.910
What's that smell on you?

739
37:17.610 --> 37:18.650
That Gao Fuyuan

740
37:18.760 --> 37:20.120
was like a big rat,

741
37:20.160 --> 37:21.350
hiding inside that cave

742
37:21.480 --> 37:22.560
and refusing to come out.

743
37:22.770 --> 37:23.540
So I

744
37:23.660 --> 37:25.100
used the method you taught me.

745
37:26.710 --> 37:27.840
I threw a hand grenade

746
37:27.930 --> 37:29.120
down that chimney.

747
37:29.620 --> 37:30.410
I was afraid it wasn't enough,

748
37:30.560 --> 37:31.850
so I added a handful of chili powder too.

749
37:32.950 --> 37:34.340
You brat, isn't that a waste?

750
37:34.760 --> 37:35.640
I told you

751
37:35.660 --> 37:36.850
to save more chili peppers.

752
37:36.960 --> 37:39.120
The comrades from the south love eating chili peppers.

753
37:39.770 --> 37:40.920
Look at my brain.

754
37:41.650 --> 37:42.490
When I go back,

755
37:42.600 --> 37:44.470
I'll buy more chili peppers from the locals to make up for it.

756
37:46.490 --> 37:47.370
How's your hand?

757
37:48.420 --> 37:48.940
Look,

758
37:49.750 --> 37:51.590
it can move, but it just can't straighten out.

759
37:53.330 --> 37:54.210
Corps Commander!

760
37:54.580 --> 37:55.190
Corps Commander!

761
37:55.760 --> 37:56.550
Good news!

762
37:57.130 --> 37:57.920
What good news?

763
37:58.150 --> 37:59.070
Do we have chili peppers?

764
38:03.020 --> 38:03.980
Never mind, go ahead.

765
38:04.870 --> 38:06.120
The Political Commissar sent someone with a letter.

766
38:06.350 --> 38:07.950
The Central Committee has already led the Central Red Army

767
38:08.170 --> 38:09.330
to Wuqi Town!

768
38:09.530 --> 38:10.220
What?

769
38:10.660 --> 38:11.620
Let me see.

770
38:14.800 --> 38:16.280
The Political Commissar and comrades from the Provincial Committee

771
38:16.310 --> 38:18.580
are heading towards Wuqi Town to welcome the Central Committee together.

772
38:19.190 --> 38:20.670
They also want to send a circular telegram to the Party Central Committee,

773
38:20.760 --> 38:21.910
and they're asking for your opinion.

774
38:22.570 --> 38:23.490
That's wonderful!

775
38:23.830 --> 38:24.870
We are welcoming the Central Committee!

776
38:25.000 --> 38:25.850
Write back to the Political Commissar

777
38:25.870 --> 38:26.900
and say my opinion is

778
38:27.360 --> 38:28.470
that our 15th Red Army Corps

779
38:28.500 --> 38:30.350
firmly supports the leadership of the Central Committee,

780
38:30.690 --> 38:33.170
and is willing to be the vanguard and dare-to-die corps

781
38:33.190 --> 38:34.020
for the Central Committee to march north and resist Japan!

782
38:34.290 --> 38:35.960
Great! Yes!

783
38:37.540 --> 38:38.680
Get me another bowl, quick.

784
38:38.700 --> 38:39.990
Here, I'll get it for you.

785
38:42.470 --> 38:45.950
[Xi'an, Shaanxi]

786
38:46.510 --> 38:47.480
If I remember correctly,

787
38:47.550 --> 38:49.000
this 619th Regiment

788
38:49.030 --> 38:51.200
was stationed in Yulin Bridge 5 days early, right?

789
38:51.220 --> 38:51.860
Yes.

790
38:51.330 --> 38:56.840
[Zhang Xueliang, Acting Commander-in-Chief of the Kuomintang Northwest "Communist Bandit Suppression" Headquarters]

791
38:54.090 --> 38:55.560
I know Gao Fuyuan;

792
38:55.920 --> 38:57.150
he used to be the captain of my guards.

793
38:57.670 --> 38:59.360
He should know how to fight.

794
38:59.710 --> 39:00.960
Four elite battalions,

795
39:02.230 --> 39:05.310
with the best weapons and equipment of the Northeast Army,

796
39:05.670 --> 39:07.710
how did they get completely wiped out?

797
39:14.360 --> 39:16.070
If you talk about He Lizhong,

798
39:16.290 --> 39:17.320
who underestimated the enemy

799
39:17.720 --> 39:18.880
and recklessly fell into their ambush

800
39:18.910 --> 39:19.970
in Laoshan,

801
39:20.730 --> 39:22.000
that would be understandable.

802
39:22.270 --> 39:23.940
But this time he can't justify it.

803
39:24.040 --> 39:24.850
I share the responsibility too.

804
39:25.010 --> 39:26.450
I'm not here to lay blame.

805
39:27.770 --> 39:28.890
I've been wondering

806
39:29.620 --> 39:32.530
if the Red Army is really a spent force in complete disarray

807
39:32.710 --> 39:34.750
as Chiang Kai-shek described.

808
39:35.590 --> 39:37.110
From what I can see, that's absolutely not the case.

809
39:37.340 --> 39:38.820
Whether it's the Battle of Laoshan

810
39:38.850 --> 39:40.440
or the Battle of Yulin Bridge,

811
39:40.690 --> 39:43.040
the tactical level demonstrated by the Communist forces,

812
39:42.830 --> 39:46.680
[Wang Yizhe, Commander of the 67th Army of the Northeast Army]

813
39:43.360 --> 39:44.940
and especially their combat will,

814
39:45.160 --> 39:46.870
have far exceeded my imagination.

815
39:47.290 --> 39:49.220
No spent force

816
39:49.480 --> 39:51.070
could possess such formidable combat power.

817
39:51.630 --> 39:53.030
As for being in complete disarray,

818
39:53.900 --> 39:56.200
it's actually a more fitting description for our own troops.

819
39:56.820 --> 39:57.780
Dingfang (Wang Yizhe),

820
39:58.160 --> 39:59.720
I really appreciate your straightforwardness.

821
39:59.960 --> 40:01.620
You're honest and don't cover up our shortcomings.

822
40:04.050 --> 40:05.090
I won't hide it from you either.

823
40:05.510 --> 40:06.670
We are all brothers here.

824
40:07.860 --> 40:09.930
I'm increasingly feeling that

825
40:09.960 --> 40:12.080
I've fallen into our sworn brother's trap.

826
40:12.250 --> 40:13.290
I've heard that he played a trick

827
40:13.320 --> 40:16.880
of "driving the tiger to devour the wolf" in the South.

828
40:16.900 --> 40:18.340
It's pretty much exactly what it means.

829
40:18.810 --> 40:21.000
"Internal pacification before external resistance"—

830
40:21.080 --> 40:22.360
that's just his window dressing.

831
40:22.710 --> 40:23.760
"Driving the tiger to devour the wolf"—

832
40:23.920 --> 40:25.590
that's his true intention!

833
40:27.610 --> 40:29.960
In his plan of "pacifying the interior,"

834
40:30.760 --> 40:33.000
I'm afraid the Red Army isn't his only target.

835
40:33.190 --> 40:33.990
Young Marshal,

836
40:34.410 --> 40:36.890
our Northeast Army only has so much strength left.

837
40:37.170 --> 40:39.000
We absolutely cannot afford to lose it all fighting the Red Army.

838
40:39.020 --> 40:41.310
The guys are still waiting for the day

839
40:41.640 --> 40:43.170
when we can fight our way back to the Northeast.

840
40:52.720 --> 40:56.110
How could I not want to fight back to the Northeast?

841
41:03.900 --> 41:06.710
I still remember the inscription

842
41:06.810 --> 41:08.920
in that magazine you founded, "Looking East":

843
41:09.230 --> 41:10.440
"We shall not merely look to the east,

844
41:10.540 --> 41:11.860
but must return to the east;

845
41:12.360 --> 41:14.360
we shall not stop until we succeed.

846
41:14.880 --> 41:16.840
It must be accomplished by me,

847
41:17.070 --> 41:19.070
to prove ourselves true men of the Northeast,

848
41:19.430 --> 41:21.530
and true modern revolutionary soldiers."

849
41:25.920 --> 41:27.320
When I was in Chengdu,

850
41:27.490 --> 41:28.890
that sworn brother of mine

851
41:29.620 --> 41:31.190
had tears in his eyes

852
41:31.820 --> 41:33.930
as he held my hands and told me

853
41:34.320 --> 41:36.710
that we must turn the tide together

854
41:37.130 --> 41:38.400
and fight back to the Northeast.

855
41:43.360 --> 41:44.800
Thinking about it now,

856
41:45.070 --> 41:46.580
I actually believed

857
41:46.610 --> 41:49.490
the grand illusion that sworn brother painted for me.

858
41:52.650 --> 41:54.650
So what should we do next?

859
41:55.850 --> 41:57.250
As for Nanjing,

860
41:57.900 --> 42:00.270
we still need to bide our time and deal with them for now.

861
42:00.670 --> 42:01.840
Pass my order to all troops:

862
42:02.190 --> 42:03.440
without my command,

863
42:03.760 --> 42:06.020
no one is allowed to attack the Red Army rashly.

864
42:06.930 --> 42:09.410
How do we explain it to Chiang if we don't attack?

865
42:09.670 --> 42:11.150
He's sending a telegram every day,

866
42:11.230 --> 42:12.450
urging us to attack.

867
42:12.710 --> 42:14.400
Didn't I just say it?

868
42:14.670 --> 42:15.710
We have to bide our time.

869
42:15.920 --> 42:18.800
You should know better than I do on how to stall them.

870
42:21.820 --> 42:23.300
I will be leaving shortly

871
42:23.360 --> 42:25.080
for Nanjing to attend the 5th National Congress.

872
42:27.190 --> 42:29.690
I'll test the waters and see what everyone is saying there.

873
42:30.670 --> 42:32.110
We can discuss this further when I return.

874
42:32.190 --> 42:32.740
Alright.

875
42:39.410 --> 42:41.780
On November 2, 1935,

876
42:42.670 --> 42:44.840
the CPC Central Committee led the Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment

877
42:44.940 --> 42:46.380
and arrived in Xiasiwan,

878
42:46.900 --> 42:49.500
holding a Politburo meeting the following day.

879
42:50.660 --> 42:52.700
The meeting adopted Mao Zedong's proposal,

880
42:53.070 --> 42:55.110
deciding that the Central Committee would publicly use the names of

881
42:55.130 --> 42:56.920
the CPC Northwest Central Bureau

882
42:57.130 --> 42:59.250
and the Northwest Office of the Central Government

883
42:59.330 --> 43:02.220
of the Chinese Soviet Republic.
